{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1366826-how-strong-would-the-upper-demon-moons-from-demon-slayer-be-in-wod","id":1366826,"title":"How strong would the Upper demon moons from Demon slayer be in WOD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-10T12:15:35-08:00","id":1366826,"title":"How strong would the Upper demon moons from Demon slayer be in WOD?","content":"Methuselah level?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T12:58:25-08:00","id":1366834,"title":"","content":"You might be in the wrong forum.<br /> <br /> But in case you aren't, probably less so than a Requiem methuselah who has maintained their power. Folk like Zagreus are incredibly powerful and it looks like the Upper Moons are pretty mortal (in terms of dying). Probably something more like a Power Attribute 6-8, with other stats appropriate considering the level of power involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T16:57:37-08:00","id":1366882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1366826-how-strong-would-the-upper-demon-moons-from-demon-slayer-be-in-wod?p=1366834#post1366834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might be in the wrong forum.<br /> <br /> But in case you aren't, probably less so than a Requiem methuselah who has maintained their power. Folk like Zagreus are incredibly powerful and it looks like the Upper Moons are pretty mortal (in terms of dying). Probably something more like a Power Attribute 6-8, with other stats appropriate considering the level of power involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>What forum should I be in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T17:07:36-08:00","id":1366884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1366826-how-strong-would-the-upper-demon-moons-from-demon-slayer-be-in-wod?p=1366882#post1366882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What forum should I be in?</div> </div> </div> </div>The <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness\">World of Darkness one</a>.<br /> <br /> This is the Chronicles of Darkness forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T19:40:34-08:00","id":1366909,"title":"","content":"Worth clarifying:<br /> <br /> Methuselah's aren't really a thing in Chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T20:05:04-08:00","id":1366910,"title":"","content":"Not the way I -think- Magicballz was implying, where they're part of a certain generation, but in Requiem they're just vampires who've been around for at least 1000 years, or back in Rome some of the progenitors from the Middle East who didn't lose memory through torpor. It's also one of the nicknames of the aforementioned Zagreus, one of the more powerful (though well over a thousand years of age) vampires depicted in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T20:35:17-08:00","id":1366914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1366826-how-strong-would-the-upper-demon-moons-from-demon-slayer-be-in-wod?p=1366910#post1366910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not the way I -think- Magicballz was implying, where they're part of a certain generation, but in Requiem they're just vampires who've been around for at least 1000 years, or back in Rome some of the progenitors from the Middle East who didn't lose memory through torpor.</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>is</i> worth noting that Methuselahs also don't lose Blood Potency with torpor, which sets them apart from other ancients, but yeah, there's nothing inherent in having partially escaped vampirism's ebb and flow that makes a Methuselah &quot;strong.&quot;<br /> <br /> Selective pressures are liable to make the ones who survive particularly canny, secretive, and prudent, but you can have those qualities as a BP3 ancilla with no especially flashy magic tricks up your sleeve, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}